          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %em Doplicher-Roberts reconstruction theorem
            allows one to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reconstruction+theorem"} reconstruct
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+group"} compact topological group
            or “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergroup"}> supergroup
            ” (here essentially:
            = succeed "-graded" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}/2
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+representations"} category of representations
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extra+structure"} extra structure
            on this
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tannaka+duality"} Tannaka duality
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Deligne%27s+theorem+on+tensor+categories"} Deligne's theorem on tensor categories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
            (“
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+functor"}> fiber functor
            ”) from the category of representations to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/VectorSpaces"} VectorSpaces
          %p
            This result is named after
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sergio+Doplicher"} Sergio Doplicher
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Roberts"} John Roberts
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+quantum+field+theory"} algebraic quantum field theory
            as an intrinsic characterization of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superselection+sectors"} superselection sectors
            of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theory"} quantum field theory
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/DHR+superselection+theory"} DHR superselection theory
            for more on this aspect. A simplified and self-contained proof was given in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Mueger06"} Müger 06
          %p
            In brief, the DR reconstruction theorem says that every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+category"} tensor
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/star-category"} star-category
            with conjugates,
            = succeed "," do
